[0m$ [0mSHA=32e320ffde4b9ac7c621252d169fe5f46c2cc314; gh issue comment 32 --repo AgentsLoop/PlayGround --body "## Verification complete — STRIKEPOINT serves from root on port 3000

**Summary:** Playable entrypoint now at \`./index.html\` (root copy of the verified game: Three.js r160 vendored in \`./lib\`, Sketchfab soldier GLB in \`./public\`). App server runs in tmux session **app-server** on **port 3000** (\`GET /index.html\` → 200, correct title). Fixed one browser failure found in testing: pointer-lock promise rejection in headless/denied contexts is now caught (\`lock()\` hardened in both \`game.js\` copies).

**Game:** serve the repo root on port 3000 (tmux \`app-server\`) and open http://127.0.0.1:3000/index.html — click DEPLOY to play (WASD/mouse/LMB/RMB/R/Shift/Space/F).
**Final commit:** https://github.com/AgentsLoop/PlayGround/commit/$SHA (pushed to \`opencode/34010515573\`; no PR created — workflow owns it)
**Test status:** node syntax check OK; real headless-Chromium suite on port 3000: menu 200 + title OK, click-through DEPLOY → state=play with 4 bots, autostart run → kills scored, GLB soldier loaded, wave progression; **0 console/page errors** after the lock fix.
**Known limitations:** Stylized low-poly visuals (not literal CoD parity); pointer lock needs a real user gesture (headless uses ?autostart demo mode); no multiplayer.

